import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const d=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 352 | Perfect-Work Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Shi Hao's Absence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 352 | Perfect-Work Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Shi Hao's Absence","no":352,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Perfect World","Quest Sediment Domain","Simulation Review","Shi Hao's Absence","Civilization Collapse"],"related":["09-Reality-as-Basis Fundamental Stance","29-Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System","21-Symbiotic Network Operating Principle"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0352_模块2-完美世界-石昊缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md","filePath":"en/0352_模块2-完美世界-石昊缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md"}`),o={name:"en/0352_模块2-完美世界-石昊缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md"};function s(r,e,l,h,c,u){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-352-perfect-work-quest-sediment-domain-review-civilization-collapse-simulation-after-shi-hao-s-absence" tabindex="-1">Entry 352 | Perfect-Work Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Shi Hao&#39;s Absence <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-352-perfect-work-quest-sediment-domain-review-civilization-collapse-simulation-after-shi-hao-s-absence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 352 | Perfect-Work Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Shi Hao&#39;s Absence&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Perfect-Work Full Decomposition (Entry 29 · Review) | Benchmark base: Documents 09, 29, 21</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-toss-shi-hao-is-gone-into-the-simulation-box-—-what-happens-to-civilization" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Toss &quot;Shi Hao is gone&quot; into the simulation box — what happens to civilization? <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-toss-shi-hao-is-gone-into-the-simulation-box-—-what-happens-to-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Toss &quot;Shi Hao is gone&quot; into the simulation box — what happens to civilization?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This entry is this series&#39; core Quest Sediment Domain simulation review report. The preceding entries have been doing qualitative critique; this entry uses the Quest Sediment Domain (this system&#39;s general simulation environment) to give quantitative deduction: if Shi Hao is absent while alone fighting the dark source, where does Perfect-Work civilization head? This entry takes the six top-level axioms as base — anti-predation axiom, republican axiom of Myriad Races, collective ascension axiom, causal self-discipline axiom, law-first axiom (core), universal equal infinite law — to present the review process. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Protagonist uniqueness dependency verdict: <strong>Shi Hao = extreme-leaning-medium / single-log tendency</strong>.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-simulation-prerequisite" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Simulation Prerequisite) <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-simulation-prerequisite" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Simulation Prerequisite)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Simulation prerequisite parameters: while Shi Hao is present, Emperor Immortal-tier energy is almost all pressed at the front; institutional-construction energy is nearly zero. This means after his absence, civilization has no energy reserve to take over.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-simulation-scenario" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Simulation Scenario) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-simulation-scenario" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Simulation Scenario)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After the Quest Sediment Domain replicates Perfect-Work parameters, inject the variable &quot;Shi Hao alone fighting dies at the dark source,&quot; observe a three-stage collapse:</p><ol><li><strong>Immediate vacuum (within a century)</strong>: no one alone blocks the dark source; darkness pours out in full force; Nine Heavens and Ten Earths and the Immortal Realm simultaneously in crisis</li><li><strong>Night-watch fault (within a millennium)</strong>: no rotating night watchmen; Myriad-Realms strong ones fight on their own, defeated one by one</li><li><strong>Civilizational ebb (within ten thousand years)</strong>: knowledge buried with strong ones; civilization retreats to savage era</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-simulation-conclusion" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Simulation Conclusion) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-simulation-conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Simulation Conclusion)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The review confirms: the stronger Shi Hao, the deeper civilization&#39;s dependence on him, the more thorough the collapse after his absence. This is not Shi Hao&#39;s fault, but single-log structure&#39;s inevitability — betting civilization on one person is betting on a lone log that may break at any time.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative-control-simulation" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative (Control Simulation) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative-control-simulation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative (Control Simulation)&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Simulation Scenario</th><th>Shi Hao Absent (Single Log)</th><th>Absent After Anchor Symbiosis Injected</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Immediate vacuum</td><td>Darkness pours out</td><td>Alaya early warning, collective disposal</td></tr><tr><td>Night-watch fault</td><td>Strong ones fight on their own</td><td>Rotating night-watch echelons</td></tr><tr><td>Civilizational ebb</td><td>Retreat to savagery</td><td>Order written into charter, steadily runs</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Control simulation shows: after Anchor Symbiosis is injected, even with Shi Hao absent, the civilization-collapse index drops from &quot;extreme&quot; to &quot;extremely low.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan-this-entry-is-the-review-report" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan (This Entry Is the Review Report) <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan-this-entry-is-the-review-report" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan (This Entry Is the Review Report)&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Modeling: replicate eighteen realms, dark-turmoil cycle, Stone Village and Nine Heavens/Ten-Earths structure</li><li>Variables: Shi Hao present / absent / absent + symbiosis injected, three cases</li><li>Metrics: dark mortality, knowledge-transmission rate, Myriad-Rank evolution rate</li><li>Conclusion: &quot;Perfect-Work Single-Log Structure Collapse Index&quot; — absent = collapse; inject symbiosis = stable</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Simulation shows: absent scenario self-consistency = medium-low, collapse logic clear</strong></li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high (the real trilogy has partially verified the collapse)</strong></li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: extreme-leaning-medium / single-log tendency</strong></li></ul><p>Add one layer: the three-stage collapse in the simulation box has actually been partially verified in the real trilogy. After Shi Hao&#39;s single-handed autocracy, darkness returns in the Ye-Fan era, weirdness re-arises in the Sacred Ruins era — these are the literary projections of the night-watch fault and civilizational ebb. The simulation&#39;s value is turning this vague unease into a collapse curve that can be read along the time axis.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: after absence civilization has no energy reserve</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: single log outsources civilization&#39;s lifeline to one person</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo absence collapses fast but small in scope; Shi-Hao absence collapses at civilization scale</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: after absence Myriad Ranks bear the brunt</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: simulation proves single log cannot survive cross-era</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="supplementary-analysis-alternative-to-the-collapse-simulation" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Analysis: Alternative to the Collapse Simulation <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-analysis-alternative-to-the-collapse-simulation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Analysis: Alternative to the Collapse Simulation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The civilization-collapse simulation after Shi Hao&#39;s absence, after multi-round Alaya Network runs, concludes: injecting Anchor Symbiotic institutions can drop the collapse probability from 95% to 5%. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-first axiom is the core of institutional injection — switching civilization operation from personal will to the law network. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s Myriad Ranks republicanism, Alaya Network supervision, universal equal infinite law — the three-piece set — is simultaneously injected, ensuring civilization self-maintains after any individual&#39;s absence.</p><h2 id="supplementary-analysis-key-variables-of-the-collapse-simulation" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Analysis: Key Variables of the Collapse Simulation <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-analysis-key-variables-of-the-collapse-simulation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Analysis: Key Variables of the Collapse Simulation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In the civilization-collapse simulation after Shi Hao&#39;s absence, the Alaya Network identifies three key variables: institutional hardening degree, Myriad-Rank coverage ratio, knowledge-sharing level. After Anchor Symbiotic institutions are injected, the three variables simultaneously improve — institutional hardening presses SPDCI from 0.95 to 0.4, Myriad-Rank coverage to 0.2, knowledge sharing to 0.05. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s law-first axiom ensures the three improvements reinforce each other rather than working separately. The universal equal infinite law is the starting point of improvement: 99% Myriad-Rank participation is itself the best civilization insurance.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Shi Hao&#39;s absence in the simulation box is the rehearsal of darkness repeatedly returning in the real trilogy. The conclusion is cold and clear: single-log civilization&#39;s resilience equals that lone log&#39;s resilience — once it breaks, the whole civilization breaks with it.</p><p>In the final analysis, Perfect World · civilization collapse simulation after Shi Hao&#39;s absence described in this document is no isolated case — it runs within Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s overall coordinates; its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./326_模块2-完美世界-石昊之后文明即断代.html">Entry 326 · Inevitable Historical Regression</a> · <a href="./353_模块2-完美世界-锚点共生注入完美世界.html">Entry 353 · Institutional Alternative Benefit</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">29-Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const p=i(o,[["render",s]]);export{d as __pageData,p as default};
